H3500.definition:
the same as H3499 (יֶתֶר);
Jether, the name of five or six Israelites and of one Midianite
KJV: Jether, Jethro. Compare H3503 (יִתְרוֹ).

H3501.definition:
by variation for H3502 (יִתְרָה);
Jithra, an Israelite (or Ishmaelite)
KJV: Ithra.

H3502.definition:
feminine of H3499 (יֶתֶר);
properly, excellence, i.e. (by implication) wealth
KJV: abundance, riches.

H3503.definition:
from H3499 (יֶתֶר) with pron. suffix; his excellence;
Jethro, Moses' father-in-law
KJV: Jethro. Compare H3500 (יֶתֶר).

H3504.definition:
from H3498 (יָתַר);
preeminence, gain
KJV: better, excellency(-leth), profit(-able).

H3505.definition:
patronymically from H3500 (יֶתֶר);
a Jithrite or descendant of Jether
KJV: Ithrite.

H3506.definition:
from H3498 (יָתַר); excellent;
Jithran, the name of an Edomite and of an Israelite
KJV: Ithran.

H3507.definition:
from H3499 (יֶתֶר) and H5971 (עַם); excellence of people;
Jithream, a son of David
KJV: Ithream.

H3508.definition:
feminine active participle of H3498 (יָתַר);
the lobe or flap of the liver (as if redundant or outhanging)
KJV: caul.

H3509.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Jetheth, an Edomite
KJV: Jetheth. k

H3510.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to feel pain; by implication, to grieve; figuratively, to spoil
KJV: grieving, mar, have pain, make sad (sore), (be) sorrowful.

H3511.definition:
from H3510 (כָּאַב);
suffering (physical or mental), adversity
KJV: grief, pain, sorrow.

H3512.definition:
a primitive root;
to despond; causatively, to deject
KJV: broken, be grieved, make sad.

H3513.definition:
or כָּבֵד; a primitive root;
to be heavy, i.e. in a bad sense (burdensome, severe, dull) or in a good sense (numerous, rich, honorable; causatively, to make weighty (in the same two senses)
KJV: abounding with, more grievously afflict, boast, be chargeable, [idiom] be dim, glorify, be (make) glorious (things), glory, (very) great, be grievous, harden, be (make) heavy, be heavier, lay heavily, (bring to, come to, do, get, be had in) honour (self), (be) honourable (man), lade, [idiom] more be laid, make self many, nobles, prevail, promote (to honour), be rich, be (go) sore, stop.

H3514.definition:
from H3513 (כָּבַד);
weight, multitude, vehemence
KJV: grievousness, heavy, great number.

H3515.definition:
from H3513 (כָּבַד);
heavy; figuratively in a good sense (numerous) or in a bad sense (severe, difficult, stupid)
KJV: (so) great, grievous, hard(-ened), (too) heavy(-ier), laden, much, slow, sore, thick.

H3516.definition:
the same as H3515 (כָּבֵד);
the liver (as the heaviest of the viscera)
KJV: liver.

H3517.definition:
feminine of H3515 (כָּבֵד);
difficulty
KJV: [idiom] heavily.

H3518.definition:
a primitive root;
to expire or (causatively) to extinguish (fire, light, anger)
KJV: go (put) out, quench.

H3519.definition:
rarely כָּבֹד; from H3513 (כָּבַד);
properly, weight, but only figuratively in a good sense, splendor or copiousness
KJV: glorious(-ly), glory, honour(-able).

H3520.definition:
irregular feminine passive participle of H3513 (כָּבַד);
weightiness, i.e. magnificence, wealth
KJV: carriage, all glorious, stately.

H3521.definition:
from the same as H3525 (כֶּבֶל) in the sense of limitation; sterile;
Cabul, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Cabul.

H3522.definition:
from an unused root meaning to heap up; hilly;
Cabon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Cabbon.

H3523.definition:
from H3527 (כָּבַר) in the original sense of plaiting;
a matrass (of intertwined materials)
KJV: pillow.

H3524.definition:
from H3527 (כָּבַר);
vast, whether in extent (figuratively, of power, mighty; of time, aged), or in number, many
KJV: [phrase] feeble, mighty, most, much, strong, valiant.

H3525.definition:
from an unused root meaning to twine or braid together;
a fetter
KJV: fetter.

H3526.definition:
a primitive root;
to trample; hence, to wash (properly, by stamping with the feet), whether literal (including the fulling process) or figurative
KJV: fuller, wash(-ing).

H3527.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to plait together, i.e. (figuratively) to augment (especially in number or quantity, to accumulate)
KJV: in abundance, multiply.

H3528.definition:
from H3527 (כָּבַר);
properly, extent of time, i.e. a great while; hence, long ago, formerly, hitherto
KJV: already, (seeing that which), now.

H3529.definition:
the same as H3528 (כְּבָר); length;
Kebar, a river of Mesopotamia
KJV: Chebar. Compare H2249 (חָבוֹר).

H3530.definition:
feminine of H3528 (כְּבָר);
properly, length, i.e. a measure (of uncertain dimension)
KJV: [idiom] little.

H3531.definition:
from H3527 (כָּבַר) in its original sense;
a sieve (as netted)
KJV: sieve.

H3532.definition:
from an unused root meaning to dominate;
a ram (just old enough to butt)
KJV: lamb, sheep.

H3533.definition:
a primitive root;
to tread down; hence, negatively, to disregard; positively, to conquer, subjugate, violate
KJV: bring into bondage, force, keep under, subdue, bring into subjection.

H3534.definition:
from H3533 (כָּבַשׁ);
a footstool (as trodden upon)
KJV: footstool.

H3535.definition:
or כַּבְשָׂה; feminine of H3532 (כֶּבֶשׂ);
a ewe
KJV: (ewe) lamb.

H3536.definition:
from H3533 (כָּבַשׁ);
a smelting furnace (as reducing metals)
KJV: furnace.

H3537.definition:
from an unused root meaning to deepen;
properly, a pail; but generally of earthenware; a jar  for domestic purposes
KJV: barrel, pitcher.

H3538.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H3576 (כָּזַב);
false
KJV: lying.

H3539.definition:
from the same as H3537 (כַּד) in the sense of striking fire from a metal forged;
a sparkling gem, probably the ruby
KJV: agate.

H3540.definition:
of foreign origin;
Kedorlaomer, an early Persian king
KJV: Chedorlaomer.

H3541.definition:
from the prefix k and H1931 (הוּא);
properly, like this, i.e. by implication, (of manner) thus (or so); also (of place) here (or hither); or (of time) now
KJV: also, here, + hitherto, like, on the other side, so (and much), such, on that manner, (on) this (manner, side, way, way and that way), + mean while, yonder.

H3542.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3541 (כֹּה)
{properly, like this, i.e. by implication, (of manner) thus (or so); also (of place) here (or hither); or (of time) now}
KJV: hitherto.

H3543.definition:
a primitive root;
to be weak, i.e. (figuratively) to despond (causatively, rebuke), or (of light, the eye) to grow dull
KJV: darken, be dim, fail, faint, restrain, [idiom] utterly.

H3544.definition:
from H3543 (כָּהָה);
feeble, obscure
KJV: somewhat dark, darkish, wax dim, heaviness, smoking.

H3545.definition:
feminine of H3544 (כֵּהֶה);
properly, a weakening; figuratively, alleviation, i.e. cure
KJV: healing.

H3546.definition:
(Aramaic) a root corresponding to and H3557 (כּוּל);
to be able
KJV: be able, could.

H3547.definition:
a primitive root, apparently meaning to mediate in religious services; but used only as denominative from H3548 (כֹּהֵן);
to officiate as a priest; figuratively, to put on regalia
KJV: deck, be (do the office of a, execute the, minister in the) priest('s office).

H3548.definition:
active participle of H3547 (כָּהַן);
literally one officiating, a priest; also (by courtesy) an acting priest (although a layman)
KJV: chief ruler, [idiom] own, priest, prince, principal officer.

H3549.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3548 (כֹּהֵן)
{one officiating, a priest; also (by courtesy) an acting priest (although a layman)}
KJV: priest.

H3550.definition:
from H3547 (כָּהַן);
priesthood
KJV: priesthood, priest's office.

H3551.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H3854 (לַהַג) in the sense of piercing;
a window (as a perforation)
KJV: window.

H3552.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Kub, a country near Egypt
KJV: Chub.

H3553.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be high or rounded;
a helmet (as arched)
KJV: helmet. Compare H6959 (קוֹבַע).

H3554.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to prick or penetrate; hence, to blister (as smarting or eating into)
KJV: burn.

H3555.definition:
from H3554 (כָּוָה);
a branding
KJV: burning.

H3556.definition:
probably from the same as H3522 (כַּבּוֹן) (in the sense of rolling) or H3554 (כָּוָה) (in the sense of blazing);
a star (as round or as shining); figuratively, a prince
KJV: star(-gazer).

H3557.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to keep in; hence, to measure; figuratively, to maintain (in various senses)
KJV: (be able to, can) abide, bear, comprehend, contain, feed, forbearing, guide, hold(-ing in), nourish(-er), be present, make provision, receive, sustain, provide sustenance (victuals).

H3558.definition:
from an unused root meaning to store away;
a jewel (probably gold beads)
KJV: tablet.

H3559.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be erect (i.e. stand perpendicular); hence (causatively) to set up, in a great variety of applications, whether literal (establish, fix, prepare, apply), or figurative (appoint, render sure, proper or prosperous)
KJV: certain(-ty), confirm, direct, faithfulness, fashion, fasten, firm, be fitted, be fixed, frame, be meet, ordain, order, perfect, (make) preparation, prepare (self), provide, make provision, (be, make) ready, right, set (aright, fast, forth), be stable, (e-) stablish, stand, tarry, [idiom] very deed.

H3560.definition:
probably from H3559 (כּוּן); established;
Kun, a place in Syria
KJV: Chun.

H3561.definition:
from H3559 (כּוּן);
something prepared, i.e. a sacrificial wafer
KJV: cake.

H3562.definition:
from H3559 (כּוּן) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has sustained;
Conanjah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Conaniah, Cononiah. Compare H3663 (כְּנַנְיָה).

H3563.definition:
from an unused root meaning to hold together;
a cup (as a container), often figuratively, a lot (as if a potion); also some unclean bird, probably an owl (perhaps from the cup-like cavity of its eye)
KJV: cup, (small) owl. Compare H3599 (כִּיס).

H3564.definition:
from an unused root meaning properly, to dig through;
a pot or furnace (as if excavated)
KJV: furnace. Compare H3600 (כִּיר).

H3565.definition:
from H3564 (כּוּר) and H6227 (עָשָׁן); furnace of smoke;
Cor-Ashan, a place in Palestine
KJV: Chorashan.

H3566.definition:
or (Ezra 1:1 (last time),2) כֹּרֶשׁ; from the Persians;
Koresh (or Cyrus), the Persian king
KJV: Cyrus.

H3567.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3566 (כּוֹרֶשׁ)
{Koresh (or Cyrus), the Persian king}
KJV: Cyrus.

H3568.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
Cush (or Ethiopia), the name of a son of Ham, and of his territory; also of an Israelite
KJV: Chush, Cush, Ethiopia.

H3569.definition:
patronymically from H3568 (כּוּשׁ);
a Cushite, or descendant of Cush
KJV: Cushi, Cushite, Ethiopian(-s).

H3570.definition:
the same as H3569 (כּוּשִׁי);
Cushi, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Cushi.

H3571.definition:
feminine of H3569 (כּוּשִׁי);
a Cushite woman
KJV: Ethiopian.

H3572.definition:
perhaps from H3568 (כּוּשׁ);
Cushan, a region of Arabia
KJV: Cushan.

H3573.definition:
apparently from H3572 (כּוּשָׁן) and the dual of H7564 (רִשְׁעָה); Cushan of double wickedness;
Cushan-Rishathajim, a Mesopotamian king
KJV: Chushan-rishathayim.

H3574.definition:
from H3787 (כָּשֵׁר);
prosperity; in plural freedom
KJV: [idiom] chain.

H3575.definition:
or (feminine) כּוּתָה; of foreign origin;
Cuth or Cuthah, a province of Assyria
KJV: Cuth.

H3576.definition:
a primitive root;
to lie (i.e. deceive), literally or figuratively
KJV: fail, (be found a, make a) liar, lie, lying, be in vain.

H3577.definition:
from H3576 (כָּזַב);
falsehood; literally (untruth) or figuratively (idol)
KJV: deceitful, false, leasing, + liar, lie, lying.

H3578.definition:
from H3576 (כָּזַב); fallacious;
Cozeba, a place in Palestine
KJV: Choseba.

H3579.definition:
from H3576 (כָּזַב); false;
Cozbi, a Midianitess
KJV: Cozbi.

H3580.definition:
from H3576 (כָּזַב); falsified;
Kezib, a place in Palestine
KJV: Chezib.

H3581.definition:
or (Daniel 11:6) כּוֹחַ; from an unused root meaning to be firm;
vigor, literally (force, in a good or a bad sense) or figuratively (capacity, means, produce); also (from its hardiness) a large lizard
KJV: ability, able, chameleon, force, fruits, might, power(-ful), strength, substance, wealth.

H3582.definition:
a primitive root;
to secrete, by act or word; hence (intensively) to destroy
KJV: conceal, cut down (off), desolate, hide.

H3583.definition:
a primitive root;
to paint (with stibium)
KJV: paint.

H3584.definition:
a primitive root;
to be untrue, in word (to lie, feign, disown) or deed (to disappoint, fail, cringe)
KJV: deceive, deny, dissemble, fail, deal falsely, be found liars, (be-) lie, lying, submit selves.

H3585.definition:
from H3584 (כָּחַשׁ);
literally a failure of flesh, i.e. emaciation; figuratively, hypocrisy
KJV: leanness, lies, lying.

H3587.definition:
from H3554 (כָּוָה);
a brand or scar
KJV: burning.

H3588.definition:
a primitive particle (the full form of the prepositional prefix) indicating causal relations of all kinds, antecedent or consequent;
(by implication) very widely used as a relative conjunction or adverb (as below); often largely modified by other particles annexed
KJV: and, + (forasmuch, inasmuch, where-) as, assured(-ly), + but, certainly, doubtless, + else, even, + except, for, how, (because, in, so, than) that, + nevertheless, now, rightly, seeing, since, surely, then, therefore, + (al-) though, + till, truly, + until, when, whether, while, whom, yea, yet.

H3589.definition:
from a primitive root meaning to strike;
a crushing; figuratively, calamity
KJV: destruction.

H3590.definition:
from the same as H3589 (כִּיד) (compare H3539 (כַּדְכֹּד));
properly, something struck off, i.e. a spark (as struck)
KJV: spark.

H3591.definition:
from the same as H3589 (כִּיד); (perhaps smaller than H2595 (חֲנִית)lemma חֲניִת second vowel, corrected to חֲנִית)
properly, something to strike with, i.e. a dart
KJV: lance, shield, spear, target.

H3592.definition:
the same as H3591 (כִּידוֹן);
Kidon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Chidon.

H3593.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
perhaps tumult
KJV: battle.

H3594.definition:
from H3559 (כּוּן);
properly, a statue, i.e. idol; but used (by euphemism) forsome heathen deity (perhaps corresponding to Priapus or Baal-peor)
KJV: Chiun.

H3595.definition:
or כִּיֹּר; from the same as H3564 (כּוּר);
properly, something round (as excavated or bored), i.e. a chafing-dish forcoals or a caldron forcooking; hence (from similarity of form) a washbowl; also (for the same reason) a pulpit or platform
KJV: hearth, laver, pan, scaffold.

H3596.definition:
or כֵּלַי; from H3557 (כּוּל) in the sense of withholding;
niggardly
KJV: churl.

H3597.definition:
from an unused root meaning to clap or strike with noise;
a club or sledge-hammer
KJV: hammer.

H3598.definition:
from the same as H3558 (כּוּמָז);
a cluster of stars, i.e. the Pleiades
KJV: Pleiades, seven stars.

H3599.definition:
a form for H3563 (כּוֹס);
a cup; also a bag formoney or weights
KJV: bag, cup, purse.
